'''Viborg Fodsports Forening''' ({{lit|Viborg Footsport Association}}), also referred to as '''Viborg FF''' or simply '''VFF''', is a Danish [[association football]] club based in the [[Central Denmark Region|Central Jutland]] city of [[Viborg, Denmark|Viborg]]. The club currently competes in the [[Danish Superliga]], the highest league of the [[Danish football league system]]. Nicknamed {{lang|da|De Grønne}}, the club was founded on 1{{nbsp}}April 1896. As of the end of their 2025–26 season, the club's only trophies are the [[1999–2000 Danish Cup]] and the 2000 [[Danish Super Cup]].

After originally playing their football matches at {{lang|da|Eksercerpladsen}}, Viborg moved into their current stadium, [[Viborg Stadium|Energi Viborg Arena]], in 1931. Following the stadium's reconstruction in the early{{nbsp}}2000s, the current capacity is 10,000."}}
